{"name":"Black Leather Jacket","hex":"#253529","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"},{"term":"jacket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain types of outerwear.","A lifejacket."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confine (someone) to a straitjacket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To enclose or encase in a jacket or other covering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Black Leather Jacket","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Leather Jacket is a book written by English journalist and author Mick Farren published in 1985."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c4/The_Black_Leather_Jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Leather_Jacket"},{"title":"Leather jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A leather jacket is a jacket or coat made from the tanned skin of various animals. The leather material is typically dyed black or various shades of brown, but a wide range of color